lugins.\nplans/proposed/set-pane-palette-api.md:25:Add a `PluginCommand::SetPanePalette` that sets `changed_colors` on a pane's\nplans/proposed/set-pane-palette-api.md:26:grid from the plugin side:\nplans/proposed/set-pane-palette-api.md:36:This mirrors what OSC 4 already does but exposed to the plugin system. The\nplans/proposed/set-pane-palette-api.md:39:## Use case: dim-unfocused plugin\nplans/proposed/set-pane-palette-api.md:41:With `SetPanePalette`, the dim-unfocused plugin could:\nplans/proposed/set-pane-palette-api.md:53:- Add `SetPanePalette(PaneId, Vec<(u8, Option<(u8,u8,u8)>)>)` to `PluginCommand`\nhome/codex.nix:2:  # Codex status line, mirroring scripts/claude-statusline.sh so both CLIs read\nhome/codex.nix:3:  # the same. Item vocabulary is codex 0.147.0's; `status_line` REPLACES the\nhome/codex.nix:20:  # capacity from which the runtime subtracts its own headroom. Codex ships no\nhome/codex.nix:22:  # `codex debug models`), so without this compaction waits for the model's own\nhome/codex.nix:29:  # Passed as `-c` rather than written to ~/.codex/config.toml. home-manager's\nhome/codex.nix:30:  # home.file installs read-only nix-store symlinks, and Codex writes that file\nhome/codex.nix:36:    # copies on release. Codex's fullscreen transcript captures selection and\nhome/mcp.nix:17:  codexInline = srv: let\nhome/mcp.nix:21:  codexArgs = lib.mapAttrsToList\nhome/mcp.nix:22:    (name: srv: \"-c 'mcp_servers.${name}={${codexInline srv}}'\")\nhome/mcp.nix:31:  inherit servers claudeMcpConfig codexArgs agyExtensionFiles;\n.codex/hooks.json:9:            \"command\": \"sh -c 'if ! command -v entire >/dev/null 2>&1; then exit 0; fi; exec entire hooks codex post-tool-use'\",\n.codex/hooks.json:21:            \"command\": \"sh -c 'if ! command -v entire >/dev/null 2>&1; then printf \\\"%s\\\\n\\\" \\\"{\\\\\\\"systemMessage\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Entire CLI is enabled but not installed or not on PATH. Installation guide: https://docs.entire.io/cli/installation#installation-methods\\\\\\\"}\\\"; exit 0; fi; exec entire hooks codex session-start'\",\n.codex/hooks.json:33:            \"command\": \"sh -c 'if ! command -v entire >/dev/null 2>&1; then exit 0; fi; exec entire hooks codex stop'\",\n.codex/hooks.json:45:            \"command\": \"sh -c 'if ! command -v entire >/dev/null 2>&1; then exit 0; fi; exec entire hooks codex user-prompt-submit'\",\nhome/skills.nix:2:  # Every agent we care about looks for skills in `<home>/.<tool>/skills/<dir>/SKILL.md`.\nhome/skills.nix:3:  # Each skill in `skills` below is symlinked into every directory listed here.\nhome/skills.nix:5:    \".claude/skills\"\nhome/skills.nix:6:    \".codex/skills\"\nhome/skills.nix:29:  # GitHub-sourced skills: declare them as `flake = false` inputs in flake.nix\nhome/skills.nix:32:  # npm-sourced skills: use `skillFromNpm` above.\nhome/skills.nix:33:  skills = [\nhome/skills.nix:49:  ) skills);\nhome/grok.nix:8:  # Grok's counterpart to Claude's `autoCompactWindow` and Codex's\nhome/grok.nix:9:  # `model_auto_compact_token_limit`. Grok and Codex target roughly 256k;\nhome/grok.nix:42:  # own table -- the marketplace and hint blocks Grok maintains are preserved.\nbespoke/zellij/dim-unfocused/flake.nix:2:  description = \"Zellij (from fork with pane shader support) + dim-unfocused plugin\";\nbespoke/zellij/dim-unfocused/flake.nix:30:    pluginCargoVendored = pkgs.rustPlatform.importCargoLock {\nbespoke/zellij/dim-unfocused/flake.nix:99:          ln -s ${pluginCargoVendored} vendor\nbespoke/zellij/dim-unfocused/flake.nix:114:          mkdir -p $out/share/zellij/plugins\nbespoke/zellij/dim-unfocused/flake.nix:115:          cp target/wasm32-wasip1/release/dim-unfocused.wasm $out/share/zellij/plugins/\nhome/agent.nix:8:  codex-cfg = import ./codex.nix { inherit lib; };\nhome/agent.nix:26:  codex = pkgs.writeShellApplication {\nhome/agent.nix:27:    name = \"codex\";\nhome/agent.nix:28:    runtimeInputs = [ llm-agents.codex ];\nhome/agent.nix:29:    text = ''exec code