{"parentUuid":"0e36cebf-dbf2-4ebe-b70c-fb40168ea23f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFWQVB4u2Qayv1RxrSY1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes, and it's now set up for both. Claude's frontend-design \"plugin\" is just a wrapper around a single `SKILL.md`, and Codex reads that format natively, so no plugin is needed. Your `home/skills.nix` already links shared skills into both `~/.claude/skills` and `~/.codex/skills`, so I added it there.\n\n**Changes (not committed):**\n- `flake.nix:39`: new `anthropic-skills` input (`github:anthropics/skills`, `flake = false`).\n- `home/skills.nix:38`: a `frontend-design` entry pointing at that repo's `skills/frontend-design`.\n- `flake.lock`: only the new input was added; nothing else was updated.\n\n**Verified:**\n- The built home-manager files have `frontend-design/SKILL.md` and its `LICENSE.txt` in both skill directories.\n- The file matches the current version, which is the same in all three Anthropic repos that ship it (`anthropics/skills`, `claude-plugins-official` and `claude-code`).\n- Codex lists `frontend-design` as one of its skills. I tested this with a throwaway `CODEX_HOME`, so your real config wasn't touched.\n- The whole `thixos` system builds without errors when Nix evaluates it.\n\n**To deploy:** run `sudo nixos-rebuild switch --flake ~/src/github.com/tteggel/.dotfiles#thixos`, then start new sessions. To update the skill later, run `nix flake update anthropic-skills`.\n\n**Worth knowing:**\n- The skill wasn't installed in Claude either: no plugins are enabled and it's not among your claude.ai-synced skills. This adds it to both. Don't also enable the plugin through `/plugin`, or Claude will list the skill twice.\n- Your local Claude marketplace copy is from March and has an older version. The new pin gets Anthropic's rewritten version.\n- The `agent` user on yoloixos gets it too, because `home/agent.nix` imports the same module.\n- Earlier I said Codex can't use Claude's plugins directly and that `frontend-design-premium` is third-party. I didn't check either claim, and neither matters for this setup.\n\nOne gap remains: Claude gets docx, pdf, pptx and xlsx skills from your claude.ai sync, and Codex doesn't have them. They're in the same `anthropics/skills` repo, so I can add them for Codex only. Adding them to both would make Claude list them twice. Want me to do that?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":918,"cache_read_input_tokens":96518,"output_tokens":2149,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1319},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":918,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2149,"cache_read_input_tokens":96518,"cache_creation_input_tokens":918,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":918},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"0bdf6c90-1a5f-4ed2-85ee-b907fcc34f85","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgFWQUqym8yGgrXuPLvkM","requestRef":"dad9fc25-90ef-4a78-9c2f-3a671bda978d","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"5287241a-17e9-4594-86e3-b71f4fe9b3ed","timestamp":"2026-10-21T14:04:07.578Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","session_id":"ff4c36dc-31b6-4ffc-a570-c7ff2f63f5ce","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/thom/src/github.com/tteggel/.dotfiles","sessionId":"5177785d-cd1e-4fc5-a113-5f63d7df1406","version":"2.1.302","gitBranch":"master"}
