{"parentUuid":"fcec717d-e14f-4bff-a353-7b4f1ddcf89e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFXmMSwS6KSF5Qwo8GaU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WXs5onuuufPGfHTRiXDYrz","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Claude Code direnv per-command env","subagent_type":"claude-code-guide","prompt":"For Claude Code v2.1.302 on Linux (user shell zsh), I want every Bash tool command to run inside the project's direnv environment (direnv + nix-direnv, `.envrc` containing `use flake`), refreshed when flake.nix/flake.lock/.envrc change and when the working directory changes. Claude is launched directly by a terminal multiplexer (not from an interactive shell with the direnv hook), via a Nix wrapper script (`exec claude ...`) that I control, and settings live in ~/.claude/settings.json.\n\nAnswer precisely from the official Claude Code docs (and changelog if needed), quoting them:\n1. CLAUDE_ENV_FILE: exact semantics. Who sets it; is it sourced before each Bash command; in what order relative to the shell snapshot (the snapshot ends with `export PATH=...`); does it work if the user exports it (e.g. from the wrapper script) or is it only populated by hooks; is it sourced by bash or by the user's shell (zsh)?\n2. Hook events relevant to environment: SessionStart, CwdChanged, FileChanged (do these exist in 2.1.x? input JSON fields, matcher semantics, how FileChanged decides which files to watch), and how they interact with CLAUDE_ENV_FILE (append vs overwrite, per-event).\n3. Is there an official documented direnv recipe? Quote it with the URL.\n4. Pitfalls: bash vs zsh syntax of `direnv export <shell>` output, per-command performance, behavior when `.envrc` is not allowed, and whether Claude Code's sandbox (bubblewrap) would block nix daemon access during re-evaluation.\n\nYou may inspect local files read-only (e.g. ~/.claude/shell-snapshots/, `claude --help`) but don't modify any settings or files. Return a concise answer (under 400 words) with doc URLs/quotes, clearly separating documented facts from inference, and end with the concrete settings.json/hook snippet you'd recommend.","run_in_background":"true"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10582,"cache_read_input_tokens":182640,"output_tokens":5252,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":3141},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10582,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":5252,"cache_read_input_tokens":182640,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10582,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10582},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01WXs5onuuufPGfHTRiXDYrz":{"description":"Claude Code direnv per-command env","subagent_type":"claude-code-guide","prompt":"For Claude Code v2.1.302 on Linux (user shell zsh), I want every Bash tool command to run inside the project's direnv environment (direnv + nix-direnv, `.envrc` containing `use flake`), refreshed when flake.nix/flake.lock/.envrc change and when the working directory changes. Claude is launched directly by a terminal multiplexer (not from an interactive shell with the direnv hook), via a Nix wrapper script (`exec claude ...`) that I control, and settings live in ~/.claude/settings.json.\n\nAnswer precisely from the official Claude Code docs (and changelog if needed), quoting them:\n1. CLAUDE_ENV_FILE: exact semantics. Who sets it; is it sourced before each Bash command; in what order relative to the shell snapshot (the snapshot ends with `export PATH=...`); does it work if the user exports it (e.g. from the wrapp