{"parentUuid":"8c8d520b-8223-41aa-99c1-98fea5793cdf","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFdzo9aAPeiQVrJXuRjR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The Codex research is back, and it rules out a simple `.zshenv` hook:\n\n- **Codex runs commands in bash, not zsh.** NixOS-WSL registers your login shell as `…-wrapped-zsh/wrapper`, which Codex doesn't recognise, so it falls back to bash.\n- **Codex's snapshot replaces PATH.** Its saved shell environment is sourced before each command and overwrites PATH, the same problem as on the Claude side.\n- **No Codex hook can set environment variables.** A `PreToolUse` hook can only rewrite the command, so it would add a direnv prefix to each one. The research tested that prefix inside the sandbox.\n- **The alternative, a `BASH_ENV` script, leaks into every child bash.** It also tangles with the snapshot in ways that are easy to get wrong.\n\nThe rewrite has a cost I need to check before choosing it: Codex's approval rules match the start of a command. A prefix could stop your saved \"always allow\" rules from matching. I'll look at your Codex rules and read the tested hook script:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6211,"cache_read_input_tokens":243972,"output_tokens":12120,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":11375},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6211,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":12120,"cache_read_input_tokens":243972,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6211,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6211},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serv