{"parentUuid":"16e99612-bbea-4762-97fc-814a8891da62","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"50375f0e-a0eb-4ec4-b3e3-5e2605d74ad9","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CEZR3FVG15UvuF1PoAGVqR","type":"tool_result","content":"7\t  mcp = import ./mcp.nix { inherit pkgs lib; };\n8\t  codex-cfg = import ./codex.nix { inherit lib; };\n9\t  grok-cfg = import ./grok.nix { inherit lib grok; inherit (mcp) servers; };\n10\t  claude = pkgs.writeShellApplication {\n11\t    name = \"claude\";\n12\t    runtimeInputs = [ llm-agents.claude-code ];\n13\t    # `=` form is required: --mcp-config is variadic and would otherwise consume\n14\t    # subsequent positional args as additional config files.\n15\t    #\n16\t    # `--effort max` rather than CLAUDE_CODE_EFFORT_LEVEL=max: the env var is\n17\t    # consulted ahead of everything else and pins the session, so /effort just\n18\t    # refuses (\"Not applied: CLAUDE_CODE_EFFORT_LEVEL=max overrides effort this\n19\t    # session\"). The flag only seeds the session's starting level, leaving\n20\t    # /effort free to change it. The `effortLevel` setting is not an option\n21\t    # either: its schema stops at xhigh, so `max` cannot be persisted there.\n22\t    # Placed before \"$@\" because the last --effort wins, so an explicit\n23\t    # `claude --effort high` still overrides this default.\n24\t    text = ''exec claude --mcp-config=${mcp.claudeMcpConfig} --effort max \"$@\"'';\n25\t  };\n26\t  codex = pkgs.writeShellApplication {\n27\t    name = \"codex\";\n28\t    runtimeInputs = [ llm-agents.codex ];\n29\t    text = ''exec codex ${lib.concatStringsSep \" \" (mcp.codexArgs ++ codex-cfg.configArgs)} \"$@\"'';\n30\t  };\n31\t  agy = llm-agents.antigravity-cli;\n32\t  grok = llm-agents.grok;"}]},"uuid":"60e63902-313d-4477-8523-cf19fd1a3b0b","timestamp":"2026-10-21T15:55:26.803Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/thom/src/github.com/tteggel/.dotfiles/home/agent.nix","content":"  mcp = import ./mcp.nix { inherit pkgs lib; };\n  codex-cfg = import ./codex.nix { inherit lib; };\n  grok-cfg = import ./grok.nix { inherit lib grok; inherit (mcp) servers; };\n  claude = pkgs.writeShellApplication {\n    name = \"claude\";\n    runtimeInputs = [ llm-agents.claude-code ];\n    # `=` form is required: --mcp-config is variadic and would otherwise consume\n    # subsequent positional args as additional config files.\n    #\n    # `--effort max` rather than CLAUDE_CODE_EFFORT_LEVEL=max: the env var is\n    # consulted ahead of everything else and pins the session, so /effort just\n    # refuses (\"Not applied: CLAUDE_CODE_EFFORT_LEVEL=max overrides effort this\n    # session\"). The flag only seeds the session's starting level, leaving\n    # /effort free to change it. The `effortLevel` setting is not an option\n    # either: its schema stops at xhigh, so `max` cannot be persisted there.\n    # Placed before \"$@\" because the last --effort wins, so an explicit\n    # `claude --effort high` still overrides this default.\n    text = ''exec claude --mcp-config=${mcp.claudeMcpConfig} --effort max \"$@\"'';\n  };\n  codex = pkgs.writeShellApplication {\n    name = \"codex\";\n    runtimeInputs = [ llm-agents.codex ];\n    text = ''exec codex ${lib.concatStringsSep \" \" (mcp.codexArgs ++ codex-cfg.configArgs)} \"$@\"'';\n  };\n  agy = llm-agents.antigravity-cli;\n  grok = llm-agents.grok;","numLines":26,"startLine":7,"totalLines":294}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"16e99612-bbea-4762-97fc-814a8891da62","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"ff4c36dc-31b6-4ffc-a570-c7ff2f63f5ce","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/thom/src/github.com/tteggel/.dotfiles","sessionId":"5177785d-cd1e-4fc5-a113-5f63d7df1406","version":"2.1.302","gitBranch":"master"}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"5177785d-cd1e-4fc5-a113-5f63d7df1406","hash":"8e6491079ea0b09f7db96b12ee1b64095f5b950995de466291e77a3f34e11684","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The refresh behavior checks out end to end: sandboxed edits fall back with a warning, the first escalated command re-evaluates, and later sandboxed commands pick up the refreshed cache. Now I'll wire this in via a shared `home/agent-direnv.nix`, with Claude's wrapper exporting `CLAUDE_ENV_FILE` and `codex.nix` adding the `BASH_ENV` policy.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012HdWXmDJyFqkC1o4ZSoPf6","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/thom/src/github.com/tteggel/.dotfiles/home/agent-direnv.nix","content":"{ pkgs }: pkgs.writeText \"agent-direnv.sh\" ''\n  # Loads the direnv environment for the working directory into the current\n  # shell, so agents get each project's devshell without having to work out\n  # `nix develop`. They start from zellij rather than an interactive shell, so\n  # direnv's prompt hook never runs for them. Claude sources this before every\n  # Bash command (CLAUDE_ENV_FILE); the bash Codex runs each command in sources\n  # it at startup (BASH_ENV, see codex.nix). direnv re-evaluates when flake.nix,\n  # flake.lock or .envrc change.\n\n  # Codex's outer shell sources its shell snapshot after this, which resets\n  # PATH. The `exec bash -c` that shell ends with sources this again and loads.\n  case ''${BASH_EXECUTION_STRING-} in\n    *shell_snapshots/*) return 0 ;;\n  esac\n\n  # PATH differs from the last load (a snapshot reset it, say), so direnv's\n  # record of what it loaded is stale: load from scratch. Otherwise, as in a\n  # bash started by a command, direnv only checks for changes.\n  if [ \"$PATH\" != \"''${AGENT_DIRENV_PATH-}\" ]; then\n    unset DIRENV_DIR DIRENV_FILE DIRENV_DIFF DIRENV_WATCHES NIX_DIRENV_DID_FALLBACK\n  fi\n\n  # BASH_ENV= stops direnv's own bash from sourcing this file again.\n  eval \"$(BASH_ENV= DIRENV_LOG_FORMAT= ${pkgs.direnv}/bin/direnv export bash)\"\n  export AGENT_DIRENV_PATH=\"$PATH\"\n\n  # nix-direnv keeps the previous devshell when evaluation fails, e.g. in\n  # Codex's sandbox, which can't reach the nix daemon.\n  if [ -n \"''${NIX_DIRENV_DID_FALLBACK-}\" ]; then\n    echo \"direnv: couldn't re-evaluate this project's devshell, so this command has the previous one. Run \\`direnv exec . true\\` outside the sandbox to rebuild it or see the error.\" >&2\n  fi\n''\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BMguvNwH3YtEvP63CwcoKh","name":"Edit","input":{"file_path":"/home/thom/src/github.com/tteggel/.dotfiles/home/codex.nix","old_string":"{ lib }: let","new_string":"{ lib, agentDirenv }: let"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01D8auJWCyPKo2YNFLAqC7tL","name":"Edit","input":{"file_path":"/home/thom/src/github.com/tteggel/.dotfiles/home/codex.nix","old_string":"    \"-c model_auto_compact_token_limit=${toString autoCompactTokenLimit}\"\n  ];","new_string":"    \"-c model_auto_compact_token_limit=${toString autoCompactTokenLimit}\"\n    # Load each project's direnv environment into every command. Codex runs\n    # commands in bash here, not zsh: NixOS-WSL's login shell is a `wrapper`\n    # binary Codex doesn't recognise, so it falls back to bash. Set through\n    # the policy rather than exported by the wrapper so only commands get it.\n    \"-c 'shell_environment_policy.set.BASH_ENV=\\\"${agentDirenv}\\\"'\"\n  ];"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DAKgEX4fp5mcFHoWX9xc2r","name":"Edit","input":{"file_path":"/home/thom/src/github.com/tteggel/.dotfiles/home/home.nix","old_string":"  codex-cfg = import ./codex.nix { inherit lib; };\n  grok-cfg = import ./grok.nix { inherit lib grok; inherit (mcp) servers; };\n  docTools = import ./doc-tools.nix { inherit pkgs; };","new_string":"  agentDirenv = import ./agent