{"parentUuid":"1bd10e99-d42e-4989-95f1-3ec41fec8f80","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFgY9y4aR9ePd56XEbuK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":455,"cache_read_input_tokens":403267,"output_tokens":1504,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":185},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":455,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1504,"cache_read_input_tokens":403267,"cache_creation_input_tokens":455,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":455},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":8028,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"b458d8e0-afe0-4b9c-a2e7-ce085188dac1","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgFgY9W2FtqovWngZ6Nft","requestRef":"99ff23e8-daf1-43e0-8023-3ad967f9dd01","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"e54fb4a3-3b40-49c0-937a-1c0707603737","timestamp":"2026-10-21T16:16:49.748Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","session_id":"ff4c36dc-31b6-4ffc-a570-c7ff2f63f5ce","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/thom/src/github.com/tteggel/.dotfiles","sessionId":"5177785d-cd1e-4fc5-a113-5f63d7df1406","version":"2.1.302","gitBranch":"master"}
{"parentUuid":"e54fb4a3-3b40-49c0-937a-1c0707603737","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFgY9y4aR9ePd56XEbuK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All three are done, built and tested live. Nothing is deployed or committed yet.\n\n**Code review**\n- I removed `code-review-skill` and added `receiving-code-review` from `obra/superpowers` to both agents. That skill is about acting on review findings. The reviewing itself is left to the built-ins: `/code-review` in Claude and `/review` in Codex.\n\n**Doc skills and tools**\n- **Codex skills:** it now has OpenAI's Apache-2.0 skills: `doc`, `pdf`, `spreadsheet` and `slides`. They're pinned to an old revision because OpenAI has since removed three of them, so they won't get updates.\n- **Tools for both agents:** Python with the document libraries, LibreOffice, poppler, pandoc and qpdf. They're on the `claude` and `codex` wrappers' PATH only, so your own shell is unchanged.\n- **Fonts:** I added Carlito, Caladea, Liberation and DejaVu. Before, the only font installed was DejaVu Sans, so every document rendered in it. A test `.docx` now renders Calibri, Arial, Times New Roman and Cambria with the right stand-ins, and a spreadsheet formula recalculates.\n- **Left out for size:** markitdown (778 MiB), tesseract OCR (1.1 GB), ghostscript and ImageMagick. Say if you want any of them.\n\n**direnv devshells** (`home/agent-direnv.nix`)\n- **What changes:** every command either agent runs now loads the direnv environment for its working directory. Changing directory, or editing `flake.nix`, `flake.lock` or `.envrc`, takes effect on the next command. It costs about 0.1–0.15 s per command inside a direnv project and about 10 ms elsewhere.\n- **Claude:** the wrapper sets `CLAUDE_ENV_FILE`, a script Claude runs before each Bash command.\n- **Codex:** this was the hard part. It runs commands in bash and removes `BASH_ENV` from their environment, and its hooks could only do this by rewriting commands, which would break your 60 approval rules. Instead, its wrapper puts a tiny compiled `bash` first on its PATH. That wrapper restores `BASH_ENV` and runs the real bash, so commands and approval rules are untouched.\n- **Tested live:** in `todd`, both agents found `bun` from its devshell. In a scratch flake, an edit to `flake.nix` took effect on the next command.\n- **Caveats:**\n  - Inside Codex's sandbox, nix can't re-evaluate a changed flake. Commands keep the previous devshell and print a warning telling the agent to run `direnv exec . true` outside the sandbox, after which sandboxed commands get the new one.\n  - In a project whose `.envrc` isn't allowed (such as `bookcreator-…`), every command shows direnv's \"is blocked\" error.\n  - If a project's devshell has its own `python3`, that one comes first on PATH, so the doc skills won't find their libraries in that project.\n- **yoloixos:** it gets the direnv change but not the doc tools, which would be another 2.2 GB in its separate store. Say if you want them there too.\n\n**To deploy:** run `sudo nixos-rebuild switch --flake ~/src/github.com/tteggel/.dotfiles#thixos`, then restart your agent sessions. I ran `git add` on the two new files, `home/doc-tools.nix` and `home/agent-direnv.nix`, because flakes only see tracked files.\n\nOne other thing slows agents down: Claude's shell snapshot copies your zsh aliases (`ls`→eza, `grep`→rg, `find`→fd, `cat`→bat). That means its `ls` and `find` commands run different tools with different flags; I hit this myself in this session. Codex isn't affected because it uses bash. I can stop those aliases loading inside Claude's shells if you'd like."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":455,"cache_read_input_tokens":403267,"output_tokens":1504,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":185},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requ